        "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{330}^{\u2218})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{330}^{\u2218})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={330}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{330}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{330}^{\u2218}+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{330}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
